1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,900
When the story progresses tyler and a narrator began to see the world through a different lens.
随着情节推进，泰勒和叙述者开始从不同角度看世界。

2
00:00:05,910 --> 00:00:14,190
Tyler criticizes the modern self improvement type by saying self improvement is masturbation now self destruction.
作者引用泰勒带有性隐喻的粗俗台词，贬低自我改善，并转而提到自我毁灭。

3
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:19,400
This statement is slightly confusing as the increasingly destructive nature of fight club.
这句话让人困惑，因为搏击俱乐部的性质越来越具破坏性。

4
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:26,640
We're faces are permanently mutilated and teeth are knocked out of people's heads doesn't seem to be a sustainable way to live.
人们的脸永久受伤、牙齿被打落，这看来并不是可持续的生活方式。

5
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:33,660
But tyler might be on to something when we look at self destruction as the destruction of a false self.
但作者认为，如果把自我毁灭理解为摧毁虚假的自我，泰勒也许触及了某个问题。

6
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:42,360
Self improvement often points to the accumulation of external goods a better house a better job a better body more money.
他认为，自我改善常指积累外在事物：更好的房子、工作、身体和更多钱。

7
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:45,390
But why should we endlessly want to improve ourselves.
作者问，为什么我们要无休止地追求改善自己？

8
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:50,390
Why can't we just be happy with how things are and take life as it comes.
为什么不能满意于现状，顺其自然地面对生活？

9
00:00:50,400 --> 00:01:00,510
Or stiler states I say never be complete I say stop being perfect I say let's evolve let the chips fall where they may and quote.
作者引用角色：永远别完整，别追求完美，让自己变化，接受结果。

10
00:01:00,510 --> 00:01:05,070
We create an identity through material wealth and social status.
作者说，人通过物质财富和社会地位建立身份。

11
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:13,550
And as far as tyler is concerned this false sense of self must be destroyed before we are free to do anything we want.
按泰勒的看法，虚假的自我感必须被摧毁，人才能自由行动。

12
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:18,880
Therefore project mames space monkeys live by a mantra which goes like this.
因此，那个组织的成员遵循着这样一套口号。

13
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:23,310
You are not your job you're not how much money you have in the bank.
角色台词说：你不等于你的工作，也不等于银行里的钱。

14
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:27,910
You are not the car you drive you're not the contents of your wallet.
你不等于开的车，也不等于钱包里的东西。

15
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:34,990
You're notch of khakis you are all singing all dancing crap of the world end quote.
台词继续否定用衣物定义身份，并用粗俗话形容世人；引文结束。

16
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:43,550
Tyler makes a so called human sacrifice namely a man called a raymond who works a dead end job in a convenience store.
作者讲述一段所谓牺牲的剧情：雷蒙德在便利店做一份缺乏前景的工作。

17
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:49,800
Raymond wanted to be a veterinarian but didn't make it because it was quote unquote too much studying.
他原本想做兽医，却因所谓需要学太多而没完成学业。

18
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:56,360
Tyler threatens raymond saying that if he doesn't start studying within six weeks he'll kill him.
虚构剧情中，泰勒以杀害雷蒙德相威胁，要求他六周内重新开始学习。

19
00:01:56,370 --> 00:02:00,420
In this scene tyler points to another aspect of self destruction.
作者认为，这一场景还指向自我毁灭主题的另一个层面。

20
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:08,180
The act of letting go of fears negative self talk and all distractions so we can fully focus on our purpose.
他将其解读为放下恐惧、负面自我对话和干扰，从而专注目的。

21
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:17,470
It's the destruction of everything within ourselves that holds us back from living life on our own terms.
也就是去除那些妨碍自己按自身意愿生活的内在障碍。

22
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:21,379
Many people go great lengths when it comes to pain avoidance.
作者说，谈到躲避痛苦，很多人会不惜付出很大努力。

23
00:02:21,379 --> 00:02:26,689
The problem is that running from pain means running from an inevitable part of life.
他认为，逃离痛苦也意味着逃离生活中难以避免的一部分。

24
00:02:26,689 --> 00:02:32,720
The prospect of incurring pain makes us anxious and often leads to hedonistic decisions.
对可能遭受痛苦的担忧会带来焦虑，并在他看来促使人追求眼前享乐。

25
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:35,420
That is choosing the less painful path.
也就是说，选择眼下痛苦较少的道路。

26
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:40,780
Even if a more painful path guarantees more success and pleasure in the future.
即使另一条更痛苦的路，可能在未来带来更多成功与快乐；这是作者的比较。

27
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:47,590
Tyler durden deals with this by inflicting a chemical wound on the narrator's hand using a lie.
剧情中，泰勒对叙述者的手施加化学伤害；这里的物质名称字幕存疑。

28
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:51,200
As expected the narrator does everything to escape the pain.
如预料那样，叙述者竭尽全力想逃离痛苦。

29
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:59,030
He uses visualization techniques he learned at a seminar and retreating in his cave to find his quote unquote power animal.
他使用在研讨活动中学到的想象技巧，想象回到洞穴寻找所谓力量动物。

30
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:03,170
But tyler slaps him in the face forcing him to stay with the pain.
但泰勒打他，逼他停留在痛苦中。

31
00:03:03,170 --> 00:03:09,850
Saying this is the greatest moment of your life man and you're off somewhere missing it end quote.
角色说这是他生命中最伟大的时刻，而他却在走神、错过它；引文结束。

32
00:03:09,850 --> 00:03:14,900
For the narrator tyler has one central goal he must reach bottom.
对叙述者，泰勒只有一个核心目标：让他跌到谷底。

33
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:23,559
After putting him through suffering and destroying his false identity there's yet an other aspect that must be crushed hope.
在让他受苦、摧毁虚假身份之后，角色还想击碎另一样东西：希望。

34
00:03:23,559 --> 00:03:33,319
Losing all hope is freedom and therefore he must reject what has rejected him his father and god.
按角色逻辑，失去希望即自由，因此他必须拒绝被认为抛弃了自己的父亲和上帝。

35
00:03:33,319 --> 00:03:42,069
I quote consider the possibility that god does not like you in all probability he hates you and quote.
作者引用角色的挑衅台词：想想上帝也许不喜欢你，甚至可能憎恨你；引文结束。

36
00:03:42,069 --> 00:03:47,510
Tyler states that we don't need god that we shouldn't care about redemption and damnation.
泰勒声称不需要上帝，也不必在意救赎与惩罚。

37
00:03:47,510 --> 00:03:50,650
And if we're god's unwanted children so be it.
如果是被上帝遗弃的孩子，那就接受吧，这是角色的态度。

38
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:58,040
Thereby we lose all hope but are also liberated from religious doctrine and fatherly authority.
作者解读为：这样既失去希望，也摆脱了宗教教义与父权威的约束。
